# The Cessna 182S Skylane's checklists, written in this project's own words
# from its Pilot's Operating Handbook, section 4, Normal Procedures, pages
# 4-11 to 4-17 - the handbook docs/ASSETS.md already records for this
# aeroplane's published figures, and which was read to write these.
#
# The handbook's order is kept: before starting engine, starting engine,
# taxiing, before takeoff, normal takeoff, enroute climb, cruise, descent,
# before landing, normal landing, after landing. Its figures are kept as it
# gives them.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The handbook's speeds are indicated; the simulation reads calibrated.**
# The two differ by a knot or so at these speeds, so a band taken from the
# handbook is opened by a knot at each end rather than being quoted exactly
# and then failing on the difference.
#
# The flight model has no cowl flaps, no auxiliary fuel pump, no magneto
# switch and no parking brake, so the handbook's items for those are the
# pilot's to confirm. Its flaps travel to 38 degrees, which is the
# handbook's FULL.

phase before-start
confirm Preflight inspection complete and the passengers briefed
confirm Seats, belts and harnesses adjusted and locked
confirm Brakes tested and set, and the circuit breakers in
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle open a quarter of an inch
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Propeller lever at high RPM
confirm Cowl flaps open and the fuel selector on both
confirm Propeller area clear, master on, and the engine started
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture advanced to rich once it fires

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running and the oil pressure up
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps retracted after start
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at low engine speed, as the handbook asks
confirm Brakes used as little as the taxi allows
confirm Controls held for the wind, and caution in a quartering tailwind

phase take-off
confirm Cabin doors closed and locked, and the flight controls free and correct
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 20.5 Wing flaps set for take-off, nought to twenty degrees
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture rich
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevator and rudder trim set for take-off
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Full throttle and 2,400 RPM
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2300.0 2500.0 The propeller governing at 2,400
check velocities/vc-kts >= 49.0 Lift the nose wheel at 50 to 60 knots

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Full throttle, or 23 inches, and 2,400 RPM
range velocities/vc-kts 84.0 96.0 Climb at 85 to 95 knots
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Wing flaps retracted
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Mixture rich, or at the placard's fuel flow
confirm Cowl flaps open as required

phase cruise
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.4 0.9 Power set: 15 to 23 inches, and no more than 80 per cent
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 1950.0 2450.0 Propeller between 2,000 and 2,400 RPM
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm <= 0.95 Mixture leaned
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Wing flaps up
confirm Elevator and rudder trim adjusted, and the cowl flaps closed

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.05 0.7 Power as the descent wants it
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Mixture enriched as required
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 38.5 Flaps as desired, within their speeds
confirm Fuel selector on both, and the cowl flaps closed

phase approach
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture rich
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Propeller at high RPM
confirm Seat backs upright, belts secured, and the landing light on
range velocities/vc-kts 69.0 81.0 Approach at 70 to 80 knots with the flaps up

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 20.0 38.5 Wing flaps full, below 100 knots
range velocities/vc-kts 59.0 71.0 Sixty to seventy knots with the flaps full
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Power reduced to idle as the obstacle is cleared
confirm Touch down on the main wheels, then lower the nose wheel gently
confirm Braking the minimum required

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Wing flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back for the taxi
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Cowl flaps open
